From e373da46bd72a7de9f6b3de2801ec8083b329b9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ccr <ccr@aciceri.dev>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 12:15:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] collab-web: hold a live voice call from the browser

Adds LiveAudioDevice: microphone capture resampled to the 16 kHz mono PCM16
the host realtime peer expects, and jitter-buffered playback of the host
output stream. Echo cancellation is left to getUserMedia, matching the
host decision to skip its software echo gate for remote input.

A guest never learns its own relay peer id, so live ownership is tracked
from local intent: we claimed, the host confirmed. The microphone button is
hidden for read-only guests and disabled while another peer holds audio.

(cherry picked from commit 341ba7102000b68feb8663ac17d5c3f5c23a6a00)
